// Round 3 M. A named function that returns nothing binds R to void; the
// compiler accepts the call and the C compiler rejects `void t1 = ...`.
// (A closure literal without a result type is rejected correctly: "give the
// result type of the closure".) Must be a compile error.
// error: nothing|value|infer|result
fn call[R](f: &fn(): R): R { return f() }
fn hi() { println("x") }
fn main() { call(hi) }
